; S1a.3.1 — a nested `(or …)` in a `:match` premise.
;
; Only a TOP-LEVEL `(or …)` is supported: S1.8.A13 splits one into a plan per
; disjunct. Until S1.22.0 a nested one returned `[]`, which was silently wrong
; in BOTH polarities — this rule fired with neither p nor q in the KB
; (unsound), and its mirror `(absent (or (p ?x) (q ?x)))` never fired with
; neither present (incomplete, and permanently: the empty sub-plan makes the
; guard fail, and a failing monotone guard retires its candidate).
(relation a Thing)
(relation p Thing)
(relation q Thing)

(rule nested-disjunction ()
  :match  (and (a ?x) (or (p ?x) (q ?x)))
  :assert (p ?x))
